cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite the paper listed under preferred-citation.
  The photographs, annotations and model responses it reads are deposited
  separately; see the dataset entry under references.
title: >-
  Analysis code for zero-shot fractional vegetation cover estimation with
  multimodal large language models
abstract: >-
  Inference and analysis code behind the paper. It holds the scripts that put
  six open-weight multimodal models through a model-by-prompt grid on 1,155
  quadrat photographs, the parser that reduces each response to a vegetation
  percentage and a self-reported confidence, an ExG-ExR vegetation-index
  baseline, and one notebook per research question producing every statistic
  the paper reports.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
keywords:
  - fractional vegetation cover
  - rangeland monitoring
  - multimodal large language models
  - zero-shot estimation
  - quadrat photography
  - arid ecosystems
